WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.440
After Game of Thrones, Jason Mamoa felt&nbsp;
pigeonholed, not for his incredible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.160
physique and rakish good looks, but&nbsp;
for his grasp…of the English language?

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.260
Since Game of Thrones aired its first season&nbsp;
back in 2011, Jason Momoa has gathered a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.520
following due to his performance as Khal&nbsp;
Drogo, a warlord of the Dothraki warriors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.260
Game of Thrones itself became a monumental hit&nbsp;
as well, arguably one of the biggest shows to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:27.300
ever air. As for Momoa, Drogo wasn't his first&nbsp;
significant role, as he also played the lead in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.160
2011's Conan the Barbarian, along with his first&nbsp;
ever credited role on the original Baywatch.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.580
If you haven't seen Momoa in these two&nbsp;
early roles, or even in Game of Thrones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.180
you have likely seen him star as&nbsp;
Aquaman in the DC Universe movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:44.220
or his Apple TV+ series See. He also played&nbsp;
the famed character of Duncan Idaho in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:49.080
2021 Dune film adaptation. Suffice it to say,&nbsp;
the actor has amassed a great resume. Given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.040
how popular the star has become in both the&nbsp;
film and TV space, you might be surprised to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.704
know that one of these roles nearly stunted his&nbsp;
rise to the top — and, no, it isn't Baywatch.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.700
"I'm me. One thing. One piece.&nbsp;
One person. All together."

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.260
As Jason Momoa spoke about in an interview&nbsp;
with Jimmy Fallon on The Tonight Show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:11.880
the actor's breakout role as Khal Drogo in Game&nbsp;
of Thrones actually hampered his career, rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:16.620
than boosting it. Apparently, his performance as&nbsp;
Drogo — particularly his adept handling of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:20.580
fictional Dothraki language — was so convincing&nbsp;
that many people in the entertainment industry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.720
thought that Momoa couldn't speak English that&nbsp;
well, which "pigeonholed" him, as Momoa put it.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.040
Momoa went on to recall an encounter with&nbsp;
actor Fred Armisen. They met because Momoa's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.840
stepdaughter Zoë Kravitz acted in Portlandia.&nbsp;
Momoa said that Armisen professed how much he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.898
a fan of his performance in Game of Thrones, but&nbsp;
that he hadn't known that the actor spoke English.

00:01:37.898 --> 00:01:42.218
"It was heartbreaking. I was like,&nbsp;
'That's why I'm not getting any jobs.'"

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.160
Fortunately for Momoa, Zack Snyder was&nbsp;
an even bigger fan of his than Armisen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.240
and the director soon called Momoa to come in&nbsp;
to audition for a vaguely described DC movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.580
supposedly for the role of Batman. Weeks later,&nbsp;
Snyder offered Momoa the role of Aquaman instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:01.260
and the rest is history. Thankfully, it's pretty&nbsp;
clear to mainstream Hollywood now that Momoa is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:04.800
a native English speaker. Nonetheless, the&nbsp;
actor's ability to speak other languages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.800
especially the fictional kind,&nbsp;
is clearly better than most.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.060
Knowing that Jason Momoa struggled to break out&nbsp;
of his typecast image for years after amassing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.960
popularity in Game of Thrones is heartbreaking&nbsp;
enough, but the portrait the actor paints of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:20.400
his life during this time is even darker. In an&nbsp;
interview with InStyle, Momoa revealed that during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.600
the period between Game of Thrones and his casting&nbsp;
as Aquaman, he struggled to support his family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.220
including his two newborn children and his&nbsp;
then-wife Lisa Bonet. Momoa told the outlet:

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.120
Even while he was still filming for Game of&nbsp;
Thrones, Momoa was already contending with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.980
financial troubles. In a 2019 Instagram post, the&nbsp;
actor recalled a story from when the mega-popular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.940
series had paused production in Ireland and&nbsp;
he couldn't afford a flight home. Not one to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.200
wallow in a bad situation, however, Momoa seized&nbsp;
the opportunity to go on a cross-country road&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.220
trip with his friend, film producer Brian&nbsp;
Andrew Mendoza. Momoa wrote in the caption:

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.020
While Momoa may have struggled during this&nbsp;
early-career period, it's nice to know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.620
that the actor still looks back on his time&nbsp;
filming Game of Thrones with some fondness.

